remarks.para:
To modify the range of an object that has a range property, such as , create a new object with the constructor and desired range values and assign it to the object that exposes the property. The following example shows how to increase the range of an object.
XyRangeAnnotation1.XRange = New NationalInstruments.UI.Range(XyRangeAnnotation1.XRange.Minimum, XyRangeAnnotation1.XRange.Maximum + 100)
xyRangeAnnotation1.XRange = new NationalInstruments.UI.Range(xyRangeAnnotation1.XRange.Minimum, xyRangeAnnotation1.XRange.Maximum + 100);

member.remarks:
To change the minimum value of an existing object, create a new object with the desired values, as shown in the following example.
currentRange = New NationalInstruments.UI.Range(Double.NegativeInfinity, currentRange.Maximum)
currentRange = new NationalInstruments.UI.Range(Double.NegativeInfinity, currentRange.Maximum);

To change the minimum value of an existing object, create a new object with the desired values, as shown in the following example.
currentRange = New NationalInstruments.UI.Range(DateTime.MinValue, currentRange.MaximumDateTime)
currentRange = new NationalInstruments.UI.Range(DateTime.MinValue, currentRange.MaximumDateTime);

To change the maximum value of an existing object, create a new object with the desired values as shown in the following example.
currentRange = New NationalInstruments.UI.Range(currentRange.Minimum, Double.PositiveInfinity)
currentRange = new NationalInstruments.UI.Range(currentRange.Minimum, Double.PositiveInfinity);

To change the maximum value of an existing object, create a new object with the desired values, as shown in the following example.
currentRange = New NationalInstruments.UI.Range(currentRange.MinimumDateTime, DateTime.MaxValue)
currentRange = new NationalInstruments.UI.Range(currentRange.MinimumDateTime, DateTime.MaxValue);

